---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Carousel from "../components/Carousel.astro";

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<Layout>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Harborage Marina Lease Extension Referendum</h1>
        <p class="eyebrow">St. Petersburg Citywide Referendum | November 3, 2026</p>

        <h3>What voters are deciding</h3>
        <p>
          St. Petersburg voters will decide whether City Council may approve an
          amendment to the lease of City-owned submerged lands at Harborage
          Marina.
        </p>
        <p>
          The proposed amendment would establish a new 30-year lease term and
          require Harborage Marina to construct 200 linear feet of docks, boat
          lifts, and expanded restrooms at no cost to the City. The required
          improvements would become City property at the end of the lease.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="#ballot">Read the Official Ballot Language</a>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-cta">
        <h2>Ballot Question 2</h2>
        <p class="hero-cta-lead">Vote</p>
        <span class="ballot-option"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>YES</span>
        <ul class="hero-cta-points">
          <li>No cost to taxpayers</li>
          <li>Good for St. Pete</li>
          <li>Good for the future</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Approximately $2.15 Million in Planned Improvements</h2>
      <p>
        Harborage Marina states that a new 30-year term would make a major
        investment in the nearly 40-year-old facility financially feasible. Its
        April 2026 presentation identifies approximately $2.15 million in
        planned improvements.
      </p>

      <ul class="costs">
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">$1 Million</span>
          <span class="cost-title">New Dock</span>
          Approximately 200 linear feet of new dock with fire suppression,
          water, and electrical service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">$650,000</span>
          <span class="cost-title">Boat Lifts</span>
          Installation of boat lifts intended to accommodate additional boaters
          and larger vessels.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">$500,000</span>
          <span class="cost-title">Expanded Restrooms</span>
          Expansion and improvement of restroom facilities.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="note" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        The approximately $2.15 million figure is Harborage Marina's estimated
        investment. The ballot requires the specified improvements but does not
        establish a $2.15 million minimum expenditure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Why a 30-Year Term?</h2>
      <p>
        Harborage Marina requested a new 30-year lease term in November 2025 to
        support additional investment in the marina. The presentation states
        that the proposed term would make the multi-million-dollar investment
        required for expansion and improvements financially feasible.
      </p>
      <p>
        The referendum concerns a lease of City-owned submerged lands. It does
        not transfer ownership of those lands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <Carousel />

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Harborage Marina and the City</h2>
      <p>
        The marina's lease relationship with the City dates to 1986, when voters
        authorized a submerged-land lease for marina development in Bayboro
        Harbor. Harborage Marina assumed the lease in 1999, and voters later
        authorized new lease terms in 2004 and 2018.
      </p>
      <p>According to Harborage Marina's April 2026 presentation:</p>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>
          FY2025 annual lease contribution to the City: approximately $671,000.
        </li>
        <li>Reported marina employment: 20 to 25 full-time employees.</li>
        <li>Reported independent marine contractors: approximately 150.</li>
        <li>
          Projected cumulative financial benefit associated with the proposed
          extended docks and lifts: $4,514,140. This is a projection based on
          future assumptions and is not guaranteed revenue.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="ballot">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Official Ballot Question</h2>
      <div class="ballot">
        <h3>
          Authorizing Amendment of Harborage Marina Lease to Extend Term to 30
          Years and Require Improvements
        </h3>
        <p>
          May City Council approve amendment of the lease of City-owned
          submerged lands at Harborage Marina subject to conditions in ordinance
          640-H? Such amendment would extend the term of the lease to 30 years
          and require the tenant to construct new improvements at no cost to the
          City, including 200 linear feet of docks, boat lifts, and expanded
          restrooms. Those improvements would be owned by the City at the end of
          the lease.
        </p>
        <div class="ballot-options">
          <span class="ballot-option"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>YES</span>
          <span class="ballot-option ballot-option--no">NO</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:1rem;">
        This is the referendum language currently published by the Pinellas
        County Supervisor of Elections.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Voting Information</h2>
      <div class="voting-grid">
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Election Day</span>
          Tuesday, November 3, 2026<br />7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Voter Registration Deadline</span>
          October 5, 2026
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Early Voting</span>
          October 19 through November 1, 2026
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Vote-by-Mail</span>
          Domestic ballots begin mailing September 29, 2026.
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Deadline to Request a Mailed Ballot</span>
          October 22, 2026 at 5:00 p.m.
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.75rem;">
        <a class="btn" href="https://www.votepinellas.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >View Official Election Information</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <footer>
    <div class="container">
      <p><a href="https://harboragereferendum2026.com">harboragereferendum2026.com</a></p>
      <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:info@harboragereferendum2026.com">info@harboragereferendum2026.com</a></p>
      <p class="note">&copy; {year} Harborage Referendum 2026. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
